  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the weekly food cost for Kory's dog? Kory's dog weighs 64 pounds. Dog food for Elijah's and Kory's dogs costs 2 dollars per pound.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 5; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"I should also tell you: Elijah has one dog that weighs one-third as much as Kory's dog.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Kory’s dog weighs \\\\(60\\\\) pounds. One-third of that is:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n60 \\\\div 3 = 20\\n\\\\]\\n\\nSo, Elijah’s dog weighs \\\\(\\\\boxed{20\\\\text{ pounds}}\\\\).\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Good, now using that, can you calculate: What is the combined weight of Elijah's two dogs and Kory's dog in pounds? One more thing you should know: Elijah has another dog that weighs half as much as Kory's dog.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Kory’s dog weighs \\\\(60\\\\) pounds.\\n\\n- Elijah’s first dog: \\\\(\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\times 60=20\\\\) pounds\\n- Elijah’s second dog: \\\\(\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\times 60=30\\\\) pounds\\n\\nCombined weight:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n20+30+60=110\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\b...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Kory's dog eats 3 pounds of dog food each week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Kory’s dog eats \\(3\\) pounds of food per week at \\(\\$2\\) per pound:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 2 = 6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$6\\text{ per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Elijah has one dog that weighs one-fourth as much as Kory's dog.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The information about Elijah’s dog does not change Kory’s dog’s food cost.\n\nKory’s dog eats \\(3\\) pounds per week at \\(\\$2\\) per pound:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 2 = \\boxed{\\$6\\text{ per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
